dxgi: log the DirectComposition bridge hook once per swap chain, not on every Present

Topaz Photo 1.7.1 and Ableton Live 12.4.16 (app list batch 1) filled their logs with one
"err: dcomp-hook PresentBase m_window=..." line per frame: 2,511 a minute in Topaz, 7,525 in
3 minutes of Live, 200-600 per Premiere session. The line is our own diagnostic from 0001 (the hook
that hands every Present to Wine's dcomp bridge); it printed as an error on every Present, wrote a
formatted line on the app's present thread each frame and buried real errors. Nothing was drawn
wrong because of it.

Now the line is printed once per swap chain, at info level. NEUTRON_DXVK_PRESENT_LOG=1 prints it on
every Present again (debugging). The dcomp export is looked up once; when it is missing (a native
dcomp.dll) every Present used to repeat LoadLibraryA + GetProcAddress.

Not covered: the per-surface "dcomp-bridge SET" line stays (once per Vulkan surface).

Lab (runtime 11.10-182d = 182 + this dxgi + the dcomp patches, desk q, 30 s windows):
Topaz sign-in screen: 0 lines per 30 s (1 per run) on 2 of 2 runs; NEUTRON_DXVK_PRESENT_LOG=1 on
the same build: 1,142 and 1,800 per 30 s. Live welcome dialog over the main window: 0 per 30 s
(3 per run, one per swap chain) 2 of 2; switch on: 1,578 and 1,591. Present-thread CPU difference
not measurable (Live 62-68% vs 63-64%). Photoshop 2026 (Home, Chepino Valley) and Premiere 2026
(Home, Waterfalls project) draw with it.

--- a/src/dxgi/dxgi_swapchain.cpp
+++ b/src/dxgi/dxgi_swapchain.cpp
@@ -349,11 +349,23 @@
 
     {
       static void (*dcomp_reg)(HWND, IUnknown*) = nullptr;
-      Logger::err(str::format("dcomp-hook PresentBase m_window=", (void*)m_window, " is_d3d12=", m_is_d3d12));
-      if (!dcomp_reg) {
+      static std::atomic<bool> dcomp_looked_up = { false };
+      /* NEUTRON: this hook runs on every Present. It logged an err line each time (7,525 lines in
+       * 3 minutes of Ableton Live, 2,511 a minute in Topaz Photo), costing the present thread a
+       * formatted write per frame and burying real errors. Log it once per swap chain;
+       * NEUTRON_DXVK_PRESENT_LOG=1 brings back the line on every Present for debugging. */
+      static const bool s_logEvery = env::getEnvVar("NEUTRON_DXVK_PRESENT_LOG") == "1";
+      if (s_logEvery || !m_dcompHookLogged) {
+        m_dcompHookLogged = true;
+        Logger::info(str::format("dcomp-hook PresentBase m_window=", (void*)m_window, " is_d3d12=", m_is_d3d12));
+      }
+      /* Look the export up once: without it (a native dcomp.dll) every Present repeated
+       * LoadLibraryA + GetProcAddress. */
+      if (!dcomp_looked_up.load(std::memory_order_acquire)) {
         HMODULE h = ::GetModuleHandleA("dcomp.dll");
         if (!h) h = ::LoadLibraryA("dcomp.dll");
         if (h) dcomp_reg = reinterpret_cast<void(*)(HWND, IUnknown*)>(::GetProcAddress(h, "dcomp_register_external"));
+        dcomp_looked_up.store(true, std::memory_order_release);
       }
